  "why_held": "The addresses the run had written while it read, and what they held. Orders are the whole chain's, so a setting read with another of the type's stages moved is a reading of something else and nothing in the numbers says so.",
  "stimulus": "a note held through the effect on one of this unit's own voices -- program 79, bank nought, sounded at the note named beside this. Not a signal presented at the analogue input: this unit's input reaches its output and bypasses every one of its effects, which is measured and published beside this. What the voice brought to the stage is not restated here, because it is measured in this record: the `control` block is a take routed past the effect at every rung of the ladder, read exactly as the routed takes are, and it is what says which orders below are the stage's. The survey that chose this program was made at the lowest of the three notes these records use and is a measurement about that note. It is not carried to the others -- a voice is a map of samples and a different note may be a different sound, so each record's own control takes are asked instead. Sounded at note 64, a twelfth above the lowest of these three, nominally three hundred and thirty hertz. Nineteen equally tempered semitones, so 2.9966 times the lowest carrier rather than three times it.",
